onditions of the universe so for  instance we've got a comet and in  celestial mechanics we want to expect to  to explain and to predict where the  comet will go even  that we know where it started  but turns out that this approach can't  accommodate things like information and  other things that i will tell you  because information and those other  things are not about  only about the state of the system and  not only about what happens to a system  so the new which is going to solve the  problem is um constructive theory  and uh constructed theory is this  radically new way of looking at  fundamental physics  that i  will outline in this in this talk  okay so we're ready to so sitting  comfortably we can start the story um  but we actually uh need so the first  thing to understand is why is  information strange  and well we have a little bit of a hint  as to why it is strange um  it doesn't really look like any of the  normal entities that we see in physics  so it's not um  properly observable it's not like  velocity or position  um it looks like it is uh independent of  physical details of the systems that  contain it and yet can only exist when  it's physically instantiated in a in a  transistor on or off um in a flag  in dna etc  and there's one thing about it that it  can be copied from one system to another  without its property's choi information  being changed so now i'm talking to you  the information in my words is getting  copied into you know vibrating molecules  of air and then it's kind of reaching  you and then getting transformed into  electrical signals in your brain etc and  in all these processes the information  stays the same  um  but there's a deeper point about  information which is problematic and to  understand that we um  we've got to take a tour to ancient  greece actually  right so um this is a story in the story  so this is a myth uh there's an  interesting myth which is uh an ancient  greek um  myth and it was already about  information  uh so the story is that um  so theseus um who was the son of aegis  the king of athens went to crete in  order to defeat the minotaur who was  terrible monster threatening athens  and so before going his father  made him promise that if um  he'd be successful in defeating the  minotaur he would put  white sails on uh the ship on his way  back  and had he been uh nonstop had he died  and he would put on i mean the crew  would put on black sails so that was the  agreement  um then they you know  theseus uh went to crete uh defeated the  monitor he met ariadne  and then he forgot about the thing that  he promised his father  and and so  he left the black sails on and  unfortunately um aegis when he saw that  that  you know he saw that  his son had died and he  um he committed suicide he threw himself  in the water and he drowned in the sea  and that's by the way why it's called  agency  um  but never mind that so what we are  really interested in here is the ship  because the ship  is capable of instantiating information  it's a signal it's really a bit of  information and there's a physical  property of it which allows this to be  possible and that's key to understanding  how to incorporate information into  fundamental physics  right so the ship can carry information  because  it can be in one of two attributes  white or black or actually white  sale showing and black sale showing  and those two attributes  can be copied  onto other physical systems such as  aegis mine for instance or a piece of  paper or a flag and so on  now these two properties are physical  properties of that system  and they tell us i mean they tell us  something about what the laws of physics  are because in other universes  it needs to be the case that such  processes are permitted  and if you look at them they have a  particular feature they're not about the  state of the ship they're about what you  can do to the ship what the ship could  be and in fact they are what  you know philosopher